  <!-- Pact of the Staff -->

    <element name="Pact of the Staff" type="Class Feature" source="Vindavia RPG" id="ID_MS_VRPG_WARLOCK_PACT_BOONS_PACT_OF_THE_STAFF">
        <supports>Pact Boon</supports>
        <description>
            <p>This Staff counts as an arcane focus. When you get 4th level on warlock, you also choose two spells from any spell list of a level you have warlock spell slots for. You can cast one of the chosen spells for free and other one using your warlock spell slots. Once you cast a spell in this way, you can’t cast it again until your next long rest. You can change this spells if you get new level of spell slots or you gain a new level on warlock.</p>
            <p class="indent">Also, the Staff gives you an alternative way to cast spells at a higher level. Whenever you would cast a spell using a warlock spell slot of a higher level than the spell, you can choose to gain 5 temporary hit points for each slot level above the spell’s base level. This is decreased to 3 temporary hit points per level if the spell has a casting time of 1 bonus action or 1 reaction. These temporary hit points last for up to 1 hour. If the spell benefits from being cast at a higher level, you can choose to gain the temporary hit points, gain the spell’s regular benefits or gain a combination of the two choices.</p>
            <p class="indent">For example, if you are a 9th level warlock and cast shatter using one of your 5th level warlock spell slots, you can choose to gain 15 temporary hit points and have the spell deal 3d8 damage. You can also choose to gain no temporary hit points and have the spell deal 6d8 damage, or gain 5 or 10 temporary hit points and have the spell deal 5d8 or 4d8 damage, respectively.</p>
        </description>
        <sheet>
            <description>This Staff counts as an arcane focus. You can cast one of the given spells by this Staff for free and other one using your warlock spell slots. Whenever you would cast a spell using a warlock spell slot of a higher level than the spell, you can choose to gain 5 temporary hit points for each slot level above the spell’s base level. This is decreased to 3 temporary hit points per level if the spell has a casting time of 1 bonus action or 1 reaction. These temporary hit points last for up to 1 hour. If the spell benefits from being cast at a higher level, you can choose to gain the temporary hit points, gain the spell’s regular benefits or gain a combination of the two choices.</description>
        </sheet>
        <rules>
			<select type="Spell" name="Spellcasting (Pact of the Staff)" supports="$(spellcasting:slots)" number="2" level="0" spellcasting="Warlock"/>
		</rules>
    </element>

