Pact of the Tome

    <element name="Pact of the Tome" type="Class Feature" source="Vindavia RPG" id="ID_MS_VRPG_WARLOCK_PACT_BOONS_PACT_OF_THE_TOME">
		<supports>Pact Boon</supports>
		<description>
			<p>Stitching together strands of shadow, you conjure forth a book in your hand at the end of a Short or Long Rest. This <i>Book of Shadows</i> (you determine its appearance) contains eldritch magic that only you can access, granting you the benefits below. The book disappears if you conjure another book with this feature or if you die.</p>
			<p class="indent"><em><strong>Cantrips and Rituals.</strong></em> When the book appears, choose three cantrips, and choose two level 1 spells that have the Ritual tag. The spells can be from any class’s spell list, and they must be spells you don’t already have prepared. While the book is on your person, you have the chosen spells prepared, and they function as Warlock spells for you.</p>
			<p class="indent"><em><strong>Spellcasting Focus.</strong></em> You can use the book as a Spellcasting Focus.</p>
		</description>
		<sheet>
			<description>You conjure a Book of Shadows in your hand at the end of a Short or Long Rest. You can use it as your Spellcasting Focus, only you can access it, and it disappears if you conjure another book with this feature or if you die.</description>
		</sheet>
		<rules>
			<select type="Spell" name="Cantrip (Pact of the Tome)" supports="0" number="2" spellcasting="Warlock" />
			<select type="Spell" name="Rituals (Pact of the Tome)" supports="1,Ritual" number="1" spellcasting="Warlock" allowReplace="false"/>
		</rules>
	</element>

Pact of the Blade 

    <element name="Pact of the Blade" type="Class Feature" source="Vindavia RPG" id="ID_MS_VRPG_WARLOCK_PACT_BOONS_PACT_OF_THE_BLADE">
		<supports>Pact Boon</supports>
		<description>
			<p>As a Bonus Action, you can conjure a pact weapon in your hand—a Simple or Martial Melee weapon of your choice with which you bond—or create a bond with a magic weapon you touch; you can’t bond with a magic weapon if someone else is attuned to it or another Warlock is bonded with it. Until the bond ends, you have proficiency with the weapon, and you can use it as a Spellcasting Focus.</p>
			<p class="indent">Whenever you attack with the bonded weapon, you can use your Charisma modifier for the attack and damage rolls instead of using Strength or Dexterity; and you can cause the weapon to deal Necrotic, Psychic, or Radiant damage or its normal damage type.</p>
			<p class="indent">Your bond with the weapon ends if you use this feature’s Bonus Action again, if the weapon is more than 5 feet away from you for 1 minute or more, or if you die. A conjured weapon disappears when the bond ends.</p>
		</description>
		<sheet action="Bonus Action">
			<description>You can conjure a pact weapon in your hand—a Simple or Martial Melee weapon of your choice with which you bond—or create a bond with a magic weapon you touch. Until the bond ends, you have proficiency with the weapon, and you can use it as a Spellcasting Focus. &#13;
			You can use your Charisma modifier for the attack and damage rolls with the bonded weapon; and you can cause the weapon to deal Necrotic, Psychic, or Radiant damage or its normal damage type. &#13;
			Your bond with the weapon ends if you use this feature’s Bonus Action again, if the weapon is more than 5 feet away from you for 1 minute or more, or if you die. A conjured weapon disappears when the bond ends.</description>
		</sheet>
	</element>

Pact of the Chain	

	<element name="Pact of the Chain" type="Class Feature" source="Vindavia RPG" id="ID_MS_VRPG_WARLOCK_PACT_BOONS_PACT_OF_THE_CHAIN">
		<supports>Pact Boon</supports>
